WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks for having me.
-That was you -- that was you

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Cedric the Entertainer
right there.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:05.572 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-It was, and it's funny.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a very serious
and somber movie

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I love, but it is hard
to find a funny moment,

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you found it.
-Yeah. We found the one,

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
because this is not --
-Yeah, yeah, mined it out.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.817
-Do not let the presence
of Cedric the Entertainer

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
lead you astray.
This a very serious movie.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play a priest
in upstate New York.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-A small -- in a small church

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.625
who is having a crisis of faith.
-Exactly.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, whereabouts
does the crisis come from?

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:33.066
-It comes from counseling
a young man who is experiencing

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.702
severe depression about what's
happening with the environment.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.872 size:81% position:41%
And I play this priest
who takes his crisis

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:43.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
really seriously,
and hilarity begins there.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.244 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:48.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
Laughs ensue.
No, it's a brilliant movie.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.518 size:84% position:42%
It's written by the guy
who wrote "Taxi Driver"

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:52.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
and "Raging Bull,"
Paul Schrader.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Paul Schrader, yeah.
-He's a brilliant director,

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:57.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when I read it,
it was one of these scripts

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he's just giving voice
to something that I think

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.529
a lot of people are feeling
right now -- a level of anxiety

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:05.665 size:75% position:38%
about our leadership
and about our faith

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.701
and where it intersects with
love and what we are doing,

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.805
and it was --
It blew me away when I read it.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, it's an honor
to be here.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you play a priest
in this film.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.844 size:88% position:44%
You actually had family
in your life who thought

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.546
that would be a good career path
for you.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
Actual priesthood.
-Yeah, my great grandmother

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.818
thought that --
she felt certain when I was born

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I would receive
the calling.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And I would be a priest.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember
being very concerned,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What is this thing,
the calling?"

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:35.161
-Well, God will come to you,
and tell you, and I was like,

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay. I do not want
that to happen."

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:37.730 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
"When will that happen?"
"Well, in silence."

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, I'm avoiding silence
at all costs.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was so happy
when she kind of decided that,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
well, my calling was the arts.
-That's good.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I did, when I put
the collar on the first time,

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought of her, and thought,
"Hey, grandma, I'm back."

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
"I got the calling."

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.318 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.719 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:03.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very -- I think she
would be sad that the calling

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.958 size:78% position:39% line:92%
came from your agent.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.992 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Big news, Ethan,
you're a priest!"

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:08.962 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were your parents --
when -- you know obviously,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
you found your way to the arts
at a young age,

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
were they supportive
of this idea

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.269
of you trying to be to actor?
-Well, you have to understand

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
that my father is an actuary.
-Okay.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:21.040
-He's a mathematician.
He's -- like one of the few jobs

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the world that really uses
calculus. You know?

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:28.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when I told him
that I wanted to be an actor,

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.351 line:92%
he felt the need to lay out

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.887 size:75% position:38%
the actuarial tables
on that succeeding.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.955
You know, like, let's do
the math on how many guys

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:39.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the Screen Actors Guild
make more than $17,000 a year.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:42.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
And making sure
before I chose it,

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I decided I was okay
with that.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, that's good.
-The odds were not good,

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:46.733 line:92%
but I was all right with that.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you got into it --
You got into it very young.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And now, I mean,

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've certainly have been aware
of you --

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.442 size:81% position:41%
-Is this conversation
going to how old I am?

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.744 line:92%
Is that where we're headed?

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:58.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I'm starting
at the young part.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:00.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're going to get there.
-Okay, okay, okay.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you've come to
the conclusion, I've heard,

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.419
that there are now parts
that you have aged out of?

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's awful to realize
that you're no longer

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.591
going to star in sports movies.
-Yeah.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:14.060
-You know, I used to always --
I used to always tell myself,

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.262
"I'll get in shape
when I get that part," you know,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I play a boxer.
-Yeah, right.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll get in shape
when I'm playing an NBA guy.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.267 size:81% position:41%
And you're like, okay,
that's not happening.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:24.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
I even had the thought --
this was a couple years now,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.573
but when Brett Favre retired,
I was like, "Oh, you know what?

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:29.275
I like Brett Favre. I could
really play him in a movie."

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like "No, I'm older
than Brett Favre.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm older than guys
who are retiring."

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-That doesn't feel good.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:40.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I am, you know -- I'm
putting on my coach face soon.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think,
I'm not sure about this,

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:44.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I once hosted
an awards show,

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:47.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
the ESPYs,
and I was making jokes

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.761 line:92%
about how old Brett Favre was.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.797
And he pointed out to me
afterwards like, he's like,

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm like a year older
than you."

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:53.600 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like stop acting like
such a hot shot.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. I know.
We think that --

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
We expect so much
from our athletes.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-We really do.

